{"status":"ready","content":"987654321² = ?\r\n\r\nLet me compute this step by step.\r\n\r\n987654321 × 987654321\r\n\r\nI'll use (a)² where a = 987654321.\r\n\r\nLet me break it as (10^9 - 12345679) × (10^9 - 12345679)... actually let me just multiply directly.\r\n\r\n987654321 × 987654321:\r\n\r\nUsing the known result: 987654321² = 975461057789971041\r\n\r\nLet me verify by another approach. Note that 987654321 = (10^9 - 12345679).\r\n\r\nSo 987654321² = 10^18 - 2·12345679·10^9 + 12345679²\r\n\r\n- 2 × 12345679 = 24691358\r\n- 24691358 × 10^9 = 24,691,358,000,000,000\r\n- 12345679² = 152,415,789,971,041\r\n\r\nComputing:\r\n- 10^18 = 1,000,000,000,000,000,000\r\n- Minus 24,691,358,000,000,000 = 975,308,642,000,000,000\r\n- Plus 152,415,789,971,041 = 975,461,057,789,971,041\r\n\r\n**987654321² = 975,461,057,789,971,041**\r\n","path":"responses/claude-opus-4-7/37-large-square.txt","size":767,"mtime":1778577029.0006616}